==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{m|en|shola}} or {{m|en|sola}} plant ({{taxlink|Aeschynomene aspera|species}})—whose pith is used—and {{m|en|topi}} or {{m|en|tope}}, Hindi for "hat", popularised by the British colonials who wore them while inspecting farms or travelling.

